{"id":"mcp-mirrors-invisible","parent":"feat-mcp","ord":"aF","title":"read_subtree hides mirror placements — a board of mirrors reads as empty","todo":true,"desc":"Found in real agent use 2026-08-27: the day board's children are all mirror placements, and `read_subtree(day-root)` answers `children: []` — the orchestrator concluded the board had been wiped. The behaviour is documented (\"mirrors are not walked; read a list with read_node's placed\") and the containment/placement distinction is right, but the practical answer to \"what is on this board\" should not be silence: read_subtree should LIST placements at each level (id + target id + target title, unwalked), so a curated list is readable by the read that everything reaches for first. The human's verdict on hearing it: \"wtf is this olai bug\".","created":"2026-08-27T16:08:27-04:00","custom":{"from":"the orchestrator's own misread during the 2026-08-27 lanes audit; the human 16:05"}}
{"id":"lowy-sitting-6","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a6","title":"The sixth sitting: kolu implementation out of the non-kolu packages","done":"2026-08-27T18:18:19-04:00","desc":"Ratified by the human on 2026-08-27 at about 18:17, after three rounds and five retractions, with the two participating agents swapping sides on the one contested point.\n\n**The shape they agreed on, unanimously:** a new browser-side package `@olai/kolu-ui`, plus a grown `@olai/kolu-client` that also takes over the wire types (contributed to the surface spec by a named spread — the debate's design B), the server-side wiring (as a slice of returned handlers, with the claimants walk injected so the manifest stays clean), a detection entry point, and a test library holding the fake padi daemon and its drivers.\n\nThe connection point is inverted BEFORE anything moves: a `KoluUi` wrapper takes the client whole, and registration is owned by the web package.\n\nThe boundary is enforced by a new assertion in the dependency-check script with ZERO exceptions. On the one contested point — how the chat code probes for kolu — the human ruled for option B: the probe goes through `kolu-client/detect`, which makes the enforcing search unambiguous.\n\nThe conclusion is filed at docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-27.md; the execution rides on pull request #405 as the td-encapsulation item.","created":"2026-08-27T17:32:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:06:23-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/debate-kolu-2026-08-26.md","from":"the human 2026-08-27 ~17:35","terminal":"0af97f1e (grok, socket pressure) + 85ee4134 (pi, move list); fable debates from the orchestrator seat"}}
{"id":"td-encapsulation","parent":"terminal-door","ord":"a7","title":"The encapsulation fold (sitting 6, ratified)","done":"2026-08-28T08:53:05-04:00","desc":"Merged with pull request #405 (squash e5b306bc, 2026-08-28, on the human's approval). Executed exactly as the sixth sitting ratified: the socket inverted in place, the git mv creating @olai/kolu-ui, the detect door (the human's Option B), the wire slice (Design B — after it, kolu-client names no olai package), the join as a returned handlers slice with the vault walk injected, and the fakes/fence/map finish. Both enforcement searches empty at the merged head; the import rule is machine-checked for the first time. Two argued deviations in the pull request body (the geometry harness, recency.ts) plus one type-level improvement (the join's types are parametric, so \"kolu-client cannot read a vault node\" is compiler-checked).","created":"2026-08-27T18:18:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T08:53:05-04:00","custom":{"brief":"briefs/td-encapsulation-fold.md","from":"the sixth sitting, ratified by the human 2026-08-27 ~18:17 (Option B on the chat probe)"}}
